DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  sseetteennvv()  function  adds the variable _n_a_m_e to the environment with
       the value _v_a_l_u_e, if _n_a_m_e does not already exist.  If _n_a_m_e does exist in
       the environment, then its value is changed to  _v_a_l_u_e  if  _o_v_e_r_w_r_i_t_e  is
       nonzero;  if  _o_v_e_r_w_r_i_t_e  is zero, then the value of _n_a_m_e is not changed
       (and sseetteennvv() returns a success status).  This function makes copies of
       the strings pointed to by _n_a_m_e and _v_a_l_u_e (by contrast with ppuutteennvv(3)).

       The uunnsseetteennvv() function deletes the variable _n_a_m_e from the environment.
       If _n_a_m_e does not exist in the environment, then the function  succeeds,
       and the environment is unchanged.

